{"resourceIdentifier":"4220","resourceName":"Malatya 2 Landfill Gas Power Plant Project","description":"The Malatya Solid Waste Management System and Electricity Generation Facility (4.242 MWe) is situated in the province of Malatya, in the Merkez District, Kapıkaya neighborhood, and is owned and operated by Biotrend. The facility is designed to process municipal waste from Kapikaya province, classified as type-2 sanitary landfill, and serves a total of 8 districts. The facility consists of four key areas: a sanitary landfill, a mechanical separation facility, a compost facility, and an electricity generation facility.\r\n\r\nThe Malatya LFG plant has obtained a generation license from EMRA, with an expected annual generation of 31.815.000 kWh/year. The project's initial unit was commissioned on 27.06.2021, with an installed capacity of 1.412 MWe, marking the project's activity start date. The project's renewal crediting period is set at 7 years, with expected average annual emission reductions of 68.115,23 (tCO2e). Through this project, waste is stabilized, waste storage is minimized, electricity is produced, and negative environmental impacts are eliminated.","location":{"latitude":38.381812,"longitude":38.555486},"inPublicCommentPeriod":false,"lastPublicCommentPeriod":{"startInclusive":"2023-03-20","endExclusive":"2023-04-20","endInclusive":"2023-04-19"},"attributes":[{"code":"PROJECT_ID","values":[{"type":"string","value":"4220"}]},{"code":"STATE_PROVINCE","values":[{"type":"string","value":"Kapıkaya"}]}],"participationSummaries":[{"programCode":"VCS","attributes":[{"code":"PROPONENT_NAME","values":[{"type":"string","value":"Multiple Proponents"}]},{"code":"PROJECT_STATUS","values":[{"type":"string","value":"Registered"}]},{"code":"EST_ANNUAL_EMISSION_REDCT","values":[{"type":"string","value":"50778"}]},{"code":"PRIMARY_PROJECT_CATEGORY_NAME","values":[{"type":"string","value":"Energy industries (renewable/non-renewable sources)"}]},{"code":"PROTOCOL_NAME","valu